# Episode 5 – LED Blink with Push Button

## 1. Objective

In this episode, we will learn how to control an LED using a push button with an Arduino UNO.

When the push button is pressed, the LED turns ON. When the button is released, the LED turns OFF.

This experiment introduces digital input and digital output concepts.

## 2. Components Required

| Component | Quantity |
|---|---:|
| Arduino UNO | 1 |
| Breadboard | 1 |
| LED | 1 |
| Push Button | 1 |
| 220Ω or 330Ω resistor | 1 |
| 10kΩ resistor | 1 |
| Jumper wires | As required |
| USB cable | 1 |

